          "settings": {
            "text": "Our Process",
            "heading_tag": "h1"
          }
        },
        "richtext_N9Pnfz": {
          "type": "richtext",
          "settings": {
            "content": "<p>No two projects are the same, but they often rhyme. Here is our typical process.</p><p>Everything at Studio Peake starts with the client. We always begin a project by visiting the space and understanding the client’s own vision – for the property and how they will live there. What does the future hold? Are they thinking of starting a family? Do they work from home? These are all crucial questions to understand how the space is going to need to flex and support the rhythms of everyday life.</p><p>Detailed layout planning follows, with initial concepts, samples and finishes set out and pencil perspective sketches to illustrate them. This is a fluid, iterative process involving lots of exciting conversations with the client and visits to suppliers and workshops. </p><p>The client is involved every step of the way. We end up with a vision.Then inspiration turns to perspiration as we turn that vision into a reality. We draw up detailed schedules and drawings and work closely with architects, contractors and workshops to bring the vision to life. We handle the procurement and installation, ensuring a seamless process for the client. </p><p>We know that our clients don’t do this every day – a large scale project might be something they do once or twice in a lifetime. We want our clients to love the process as well as the end result.</p>"
          }
        },
        "link_eiw6Y3": {
